  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rwanda Development Dairy Program (RDDP2) - 2nd phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RDDP-2 aims to enhance the livelihoods of smallholder farmers through facilitating access to feed, water, livestock health and breeding services, as well as training on climate-smart practices and nature-based solutions. To maximize the potential of increased productivity, the project will also support the development of improved milk collection and storage facilities, and collective marketing through productive alliances. Awareness-raising activities will be undertaken to increase demand for dairy products and nutrition enhancement. RDDP-2 will promote the use of digital technologies, access to finance, and will support a conducive policy and institutional environment to ensure long-term sustainability. RDDP-2 is informed by the lessons of the IFAD-funded projects with a strong focus on delivering inclusive and pro-poor value chain development, promoting business-oriented systems to support the agricultural transformation in Rwanda.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RDDP-2 will be implemented over a six-year period in 27 districts: 14 initial RDDP districts to further consolidate the transformation of the sector and 13 new districts to upscale the process. The project&apos;s interventions will benefit approximately 175,000 rural households corresponding to 700,000 direct beneficiaries in Ubudehe category C, D and E. RDDP-2 will target 45 per cent female beneficiaries, 25 per cent youth beneficiaries and 30 per cent female headed household. Special consideration will also be given to youth-headed households, and households with persons with disabilities, small children, adolescent girls, and pregnant and lactating women.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Project Development Objective is to enhance income, nutrition and resilience of rural households through a more inclusive, sustainable, digitalized and competitive dairy sector. The project will comprise three components: (1) increasing productivity and resilience of dairy smallholder production systems; (2) increasing dairy value chain efficiency, through scaled-up investments, improved market access, and consumption of dairy products; and (3) policy support and project management, monitoring  and evaluation and knowledge management.</narrative>
  </description>
